//? Title: Natural Cubic Splines: Moment Systems, Smoothness and Boundary Limits
//? Subtitle: A three-knot solve, the original eleven-node Runge comparison, and controls for overshoot, extrapolation and refinement order
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given values at ordered knots, we want a smooth interpolating curve without
forcing one high-degree polynomial across the whole domain. Natural cubic
splines join local cubics with continuous values, slopes and second derivatives,
using zero second derivative at the two endpoints. We solve a three-knot
example by hand and expose its actual native moment system and coefficients,
then retain the original eleven-node Runge comparison with its full polynomial
overshoot visible. Independent refinement controls separate compatible and
mismatched endpoint curvature: fourth-order behavior is not automatic for
every smooth function under natural boundary conditions. Small counterexamples
also show that C2 continuity does not guarantee monotonicity, positivity or
linear extrapolation. Prepared native evaluation supplies derivatives and
repeated queries without rescanning mutable coefficient arrays.
)

\toc

> Three knots, two cubics, one unknown moment

Start with (0,0), (1,1), (2,0). On interval i let t=x−x_i and
S_i(x)=a_i+b_i t+c_i t²+d_i t³. Write h_i=x_(i+1)−x_i>0 and
m_i=S''(x_i). Since the second derivative of a cubic is linear,

\[
S_i''(x)=m_i+\frac{m_{i+1}-m_i}{h_i}t.
\]
\alttext(The second derivative varies linearly from the left moment to the right moment over the interval.)

Integrating twice and imposing both endpoint values gives

\[
a_i=y_i,\quad
b_i=\frac{y_{i+1}-y_i}{h_i}-\frac{h_i(2m_i+m_{i+1})}{6},\quad
c_i=\frac{m_i}{2},\quad
d_i=\frac{m_{i+1}-m_i}{6h_i}.
\]
\alttext(The constant is the left value; the slope corrects the secant by endpoint moments; the quadratic coefficient is half the left moment; the cubic coefficient is the moment difference over six interval widths.)

Matching the first derivative between neighboring pieces yields the interior
tridiagonal system

\[
h_{i-1}m_{i-1}+2(h_{i-1}+h_i)m_i+h_i m_{i+1}
=6\left(\frac{y_{i+1}-y_i}{h_i}-\frac{y_i-y_{i-1}}{h_{i-1}}\right).
\]
\alttext(Adjacent moments are weighted by interval widths, with twice the sum of neighboring widths on the diagonal. The right side is six times the change in secant slope.)

Natural endpoints set m_0=m_(n−1)=0. Here both widths are one and the
secants are +1 and −1, so 4m_1=−12 and m_1=−3. The two pieces become
S_0(t)=1.5t−0.5t³ and S_1(t)=1−1.5t²+0.5t³. In particular S(0.5)=0.6875,
and both pieces meet at x=1 with slope zero and second derivative −3.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cubic_spline_moments.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::natural_cubic_spline_trace({0,1,2},{0,1,0},3);
  const dm::algorithms::PreparedCubicSpline p(t.spline);
  if(t.moments!=std::vector<double>{0,-3,0} || p.evaluate(.5)!=.6875 || p.evaluate(1,2)!=-3) return 1;
  std::print("Actual interior matrix diagonal {}; RHS {}; pivot {}; solved moments {}.\n\n",t.diagonal,t.rhs,t.pivots,t.moments);
  std::print("| interval | a | b | c | d |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.spline.a.size();++i) std::print("| [{},{}] | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",t.spline.xs[i],t.spline.xs[i+1],t.spline.a[i],t.spline.b[i],t.spline.c[i],t.spline.d[i]);
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(65,1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=2.8;box.height=1.4;box.font_size=18;
  const std::vector<double> y{0,1,0};
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<3;++i) {
    box.fill=i==1?dm::graphics::RGB{254,243,199}:dm::graphics::RGB{219,234,254};
    d.node(std::format("k{}",i),{4.*i,0},std::format("knot ({},{})\nmoment {}",t.spline.xs[i],y[i],t.moments[i]),box);
  }
  box.width=3.5;box.height=1.9;box.fill={220,252,231};
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<2;++i) {
    d.node(std::format("piece{}",i),{2+4.*i,-3},std::format("interval [{},{}]\na={}, b={}\nc={}, d={}",t.spline.xs[i],t.spline.xs[i+1],t.spline.a[i],t.spline.b[i],t.spline.c[i],t.spline.d[i]),box);
    d.edge(std::format("k{}",i),std::format("piece{}",i)).edge(std::format("k{}",i+1),std::format("piece{}",i));
  }
  d.text({4,2},std::format("Actual one-row moment system: {} m1 = {}",t.diagonal[0],t.rhs[0]),23)
   .text({4,-5.2},std::format("S(0.5)={}; shared slope={}; shared second derivative={}",p.evaluate(.5),p.evaluate(1,1),p.evaluate(1,2)),19)
   .save_svg("build/cubic_spline_moments.svg");
  std::print("\nActual forward eliminations {}; back substitutions {}; coefficient intervals {}.\n",t.eliminations,t.back_substitutions,t.coefficient_intervals);
}
